---
// The whole ledger on one page, unresolved first. Then the site's report on
// itself: the accessibility run, and how the site is made.
//
// All copy on this page was drafted by Fable. The notes under each claim
// come from the content files; where a note reads like Maitreya, it is his
// sentence, lifted from the paper page, the case study or the post.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LedgerList from '../components/LedgerList.astro';
import State from '../components/State.astro';
import { getLedger, tally } from '../ledger';
import { audit } from '../data/audit';

const ledger = await getLedger();
const t = tally(ledger);
const of = (s: 'open' | 'word' | 'checkable') => ledger.filter((l) => l.state === s);
const violations = audit.pages.flatMap((p) => p.violations.map((v) => ({ ...v, path: p.path })));
---

<Base
  title="Unresolved · Maitreya Sapariya"
  description="Every claim this site makes about Maitreya Sapariya, sorted by how far a reader can check it. The unresolved ones come first."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker reveal">the ledger</p>
      <h1 class="reveal">What this site <span class="marked">couldn’t resolve.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-2">
        Everything here is a claim about me. This page sorts all {t.total} of them by how far you
        can check them, and starts with the ones you can’t.
      </p>
      <div class="ledger-bar reveal reveal-3" aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="bar-open" style={`--n:${t.open}`}></i>
        <i class="bar-word" style={`--n:${t.word}`}></i>
        <i class="bar-checkable" style={`--n:${t.checkable}`}></i>
      </div>
      <ul class="ledger-key reveal reveal-3">
        <li><a href="#band-open"><State state="open" label={`${t.open} unresolved`} /></a></li>
        <li><a href="#band-word"><State state="word" label={`${t.word} on my word`} /></a></li>
        <li><a href="#band-checkable"><State state="checkable" label={`${t.checkable} checkable`} /></a></li>
        <li><a href="#site"><span class="state">this site, checked</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="band band-open" aria-labelledby="band-open">
      <div class="band-head">
        <span class="band-count">{t.open}</span>
        <h2 id="band-open"><span class="mark mark-open" aria-hidden="true"></span>Unresolved</h2>
        <p>
          Not done, not known, not tested, or still pending. Where the work itself says why,
          that sentence is quoted.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger ledger-wide">
        <LedgerList items={of('open')} showSource hideState />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="band-word">
      <div class="band-head">
        <span class="band-count">{t.word}</span>
        <h2 id="band-word"><span class="mark mark-word" aria-hidden="true"></span>On my word</h2>
        <p>
          Stated, with nothing public to link. Ask and I’ll send what I have.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger ledger-wide">
        <LedgerList items={of('word')} showSource hideState />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="band-checkable">
      <div class="band-head">
        <span class="band-count">{t.checkable}</span>
        <h2 id="band-checkable"><span class="mark mark-checkable" aria-hidden="true"></span>Checkable</h2>
        <p>
          Each of these links to a public record: a DOI, a commit, a certificate, a repository.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger ledger-wide">
        <LedgerList items={of('checkable')} showSource hideState />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band" id="site" aria-labelledby="band-site">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 id="band-site">This site, checked</h2>
        <p>
          A page that argues for telling people what a system couldn’t do should say what was
          and wasn’t done to it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="max-width: 46rem">
        <h3 id="audit">The accessibility run</h3>
        {audit.pages.length === 0 ? (
          <p>The audit has not been run on this build yet (<code>npm run audit</code>).</p>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p>
              On {audit.date}, {audit.tool} ran against {audit.pages.length} pages, each in the light
              and the dark theme, at a desktop and a phone width. It found
              {violations.length === 0 ? ' no violations.' : ` ${violations.length} violations, listed below.`}
              {' '}A scripted keyboard pass then pressed Tab through every page and counted how many
              links and controls it reached.
            </p>
            <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Accessibility run, per page" tabindex="0">
              <table class="audit-table">
                <caption>Per page: axe-core rules passed and violated, and keyboard stops reached.</caption>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="col">page</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="num">rules passed</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="num">violations</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="num">reached by Tab</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {audit.pages.map((p) => (
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">{p.path}</th>
                      <td class="num">{p.passes}</td>
                      <td class="num">{p.violations.length}</td>
                      <td class="num">{p.keyboard.reached} of {p.keyboard.total}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            {violations.length > 0 && (
              <ul>
                {violations.map((v) => (
                  <li>
                    <code>{v.path}</code> ({v.scheme}, {v.width}px): {v.help} ({v.id}, {v.nodes}{' '}
                    {v.nodes === 1 ? 'element' : 'elements'})
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            )}
          </>
        )}
        <p>
          What that does not cover: an automated check finds only what can be checked
          automatically, and a script pressing Tab is not a person. Nobody who relies on a screen
          reader, a switch or voice control has used these pages yet. If you do and something is
          in your way, <a href="mailto:maitreyasapariya@gmail.com">tell me</a> and it goes on
          this page.
        </p>

        <h3>What the page does for you without being asked</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Follows your system’s light or dark setting; the footer has a switch if you want the other one.</li>
          <li>Plays no animation if your system asks for reduced motion.</li>
          <li>Strengthens faint text and hairlines if your system asks for more contrast.</li>
          <li>Never uses colour alone: every state is a shape and a word as well.</li>
          <li>Works with scripts off. The coin-flip demo then shows the one real case; the map still links every stop.</li>
          <li>Makes no third-party requests. Fonts are served from this domain.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How it is made</h3>
        <p>
          Static pages, built with Astro. I build this site with an AI assistant (Claude, from
          Anthropic) under my direction, the same way the pre-registered study was done and
          disclosed. The posts and the notes on the map are my own words. Sentences
          the assistant drafted that I haven’t rewritten yet are marked in the
          {' '}<a href="https://github.com/stiFFLer-codes/Personal-Portfolio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
